# PWA Fix Guide for Your Course Portal

I checked your uploaded files. Your PWA structure is already close to correct, but there are a few important issues preventing proper installation/offline behavior.

---

# Main Problems Found

## 1. Missing PWA Icons

Your `manifest.json` references:

```json
"icons": [
  {
    "src": "icon-192.png",
    "sizes": "192x192"
  },
  {
    "src": "icon-512.png",
    "sizes": "512x512"
  }
]
```

But these files do NOT exist in your project.

Without icons:

* Chrome may refuse installation
* "Add to Home Screen" may fail
* Lighthouse PWA audit will fail

---

# FIX

Create these two files in your root folder:

```text
icon-192.png
icon-512.png
```

Recommended:

* Use your course logo
* PNG format only
* Transparent background preferred

Folder should look like:

```text
login-main/
 ├── icon-192.png
 ├── icon-512.png
 ├── manifest.json
 ├── sw.js
 ├── login.html
```

---

# 2. Incorrect Service Worker Path in index.html

Your current code:

```javascript
navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js')
```

This breaks on GitHub Pages because:

```text
/me4261/sw.js
```

is NOT the same as:

```text
/sw.js
```

Absolute path `/sw.js` works only on root domains.

---

# FIX

Replace this:

```javascript
navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js')
```

with:

```javascript
navigator.serviceWorker.register('./sw.js')
```

---

# 3. Your Service Worker Caching is Too Small

Currently you cache only:

```javascript
const ASSETS = [
  './',
  './index.html',
  './login.html',
  './faculty_login.html',
  './SDB.html',
  './config.js',
  './manifest.json'
];
```

But your app also uses:

* results.html
* feedback.html
* faculty.html
* mocktest.html
* test.html

These pages will fail offline.

---

# FIX

Replace entire `ASSETS` with:

```javascript
const ASSETS = [
  './',
  './index.html',
  './login.html',
  './faculty_login.html',
  './SDB.html',
  './faculty.html',
  './results.html',
  './feedback.html',
  './mocktest.html',
  './test.html',
  './config.js',
  './manifest.json',
  './icon-192.png',
  './icon-512.png'
];
```

---

# 4. No Offline Fallback Page

Currently if internet fails and a file is not cached:

```javascript
fetch(e.request).catch(() => {})
```

returns nothing.

This causes blank pages.

---

# FIX

Create a file:

```text
offline.html
```

Example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Offline</title>
</head>
<body>
  <h2>You are offline</h2>
  <p>Please reconnect to internet.</p>
</body>
</html>
```

Then add it to cache:

```javascript
'./offline.html'
```

Then replace your fetch event with:

```javascript
self.addEventListener('fetch', (e) => {
  e.respondWith(
    caches.match(e.request)
      .then((response) => {
        return response || fetch(e.request)
          .catch(() => caches.match('./offline.html'));
      })
  );
});
```

---

# 5. Add Viewport Meta Tag in index.html

Your `index.html` does NOT contain:

```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
```

Without it:

* mobile rendering may break
* install banner may behave inconsistently

---

# FIX

Add inside `<head>`:

```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
```

