# 7. Your App Needs HTTPS

PWA works ONLY on:

* HTTPS
* localhost

GitHub Pages is OK because it already provides HTTPS.

Use:

```text
https://username.github.io/repository/
```

NOT:

```text
http://
```

---

# 8. Force Cache Refresh After Deployment

Every time you modify files:

Update:

```javascript
const CACHE_NAME = 'me4261-cache-v1';
```

Example:

```javascript
const CACHE_NAME = 'me4261-cache-v2';
```

Otherwise old files remain cached.

---

# 9. Important GitHub Pages Issue

If your repository name is:

```text
ME4261
```

then your service worker must NEVER use root paths like:

```javascript
/sw.js
```

Always use relative paths:

```javascript
./sw.js
```

This is the MOST COMMON GitHub Pages PWA mistake.

---

# Final Recommended sw.js

Replace your current `sw.js` entirely with:

```javascript
const CACHE_NAME = 'me4261-cache-v2';

const ASSETS = [
  './',
  './index.html',
  './login.html',
  './faculty_login.html',
  './SDB.html',
  './faculty.html',
  './results.html',
  './feedback.html',
  './mocktest.html',
  './test.html',
  './config.js',
  './manifest.json',
  './offline.html',
  './icon-192.png',
  './icon-512.png'
];

self.addEventListener('install', (e) => {
  e.waitUntil(
    caches.open(CACHE_NAME)
      .then((cache) => cache.addAll(ASSETS))
  );

  self.skipWaiting();
});

self.addEventListener('activate', (e) => {
  e.waitUntil(
    caches.keys().then((keys) => {
      return Promise.all(
        keys.map((key) => {
          if (key !== CACHE_NAME) {
            return caches.delete(key);
          }
        })
      );
    })
  );

  self.clients.claim();
});

self.addEventListener('fetch', (e) => {
  e.respondWith(
    caches.match(e.request)
      .then((response) => {
        return response || fetch(e.request)
          .catch(() => caches.match('./offline.html'));
      })
  );
});
```

---

# After Deployment

Open:

```text
Chrome → Developer Tools → Application
```

Check:

* Manifest
* Service Workers
* Cache Storage

You should see:

* Manifest detected
* Service worker active
* Installable = YES

---

# Most Likely Root Cause in Your Project

The biggest problem is:

```javascript
navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js')
```

inside `index.html`.

This usually breaks GitHub Pages PWAs completely.

Second biggest issue:

Missing icons.

Those two fixes alone may solve 80–90% of your issue.
